BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Birds at Our Feeders\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T114500
UID:8f346a4ae3456169ede085725c16b559@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a fun and informative presentation 
 on native Indiana songbirds. Learn how to identify them\, study their habi
 ts\, and play a fun matching game! Afterwards\, we go to the bird observat
 ion room to put our practice to the test.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Timber! Understanding the Timber Rattlesnake\, Brown County State 
 Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T140000
UID:17f1e5e11d8c7cda0113468f9e1e425f@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look In
 diana&#39\;s most venomous and most misunderstood snake! Learn about the h
 istory of timber rattlesnakes\, including how this animal became an Americ
 an symbol in the late 1700s. Learn how over a million visitors a year safe
 ly share the state park with these animals. We&#39\;ll also discuss venom\
 , how it works and is delievered\, and how Indiana&#39\;s venomous snakes 
 compare to the rest of the world! At the end\, we will feed the timber rat
 tlesnake a live mouse. Please be aware this program involves live animals.
  A live snake feeding may not be suitable for all guests\, particuarly chi
 ldren. Guests will have an opportunity to leave the program before the fee
 ding\, if they choose to do so. The program room has seating for about 45 
 people maximum. On busy days\, it is wise to arrive early!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Snake Meet and Greet\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T153000
UID:17ad0a6c9ebe16071d065acaac544424@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look at
  one of Indiana&#39\;s native snakes! Learn about their unique traits\, th
 e threats they face\, and how snakes affect your life! Participants may pe
 t the snake at the end of the program. Please be aware this program involv
 es a live animal.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T200000
UID:95c75cde7c19b69234831ae8da44fb55@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike on the Salt Cre
 ek Trail! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to i
 nteresting views along the creek. Learn about October&#39\;s full moon thi
 s year\, the Hunter&#39\;s Moon. The Salt Creek Trail is rated very easy\,
  but should be considered moderate in the dark. The trail has some minor s
 lopes\, a short stretch of lawn\, and possible wet or icy spots depending 
 on weather. Our route is&nbsp\; about 2 miles total and will take about an
  hour to complete. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlight
 s are preferred for night vision and can be loaned to hikers on request. &
 nbsp\; Hike cancellation policy: Hikes will be cancelled if there is light
 ning\, temperatures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above 
 105 degrees Farenheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gateh
 ouses will be informed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-98
 8-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Olympic Pool parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46
  W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Color Hike: Discovery Trail\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261025T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261025T094500
UID:d424cbf9f11f345329d2626d5a7d00a1@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided hike of the Discovery Trai
 l. This is a general hike about a variety of Brown County State Park topic
 s. Learn about Brown County&#39\;s fall colors\, flora\, fauna\, pioneer h
 istory\, and the interesting geology of Brown County State Park. The Disco
 very Trail is about half a mile long and considered moderate. There are mu
 ddy spots\, uneven surfaces\, tree roots\, and mild slopes. The trail will
  take us about 40 minutes to complete.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
